      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The diagnosis of pancreatic disease is often difficult because of its retroperitoneal location and the non-specific nature of abdominal pain. There is no one test which provides all the information needed, and a series of complementary tests are generally required. This article discusses the different modalities available for investigating the patient with pancreatic disease."},
